# Sioona Domain

## Vocabulary

- `SignalType`: `lead` | `retention` | `upsell`
- `FeedbackLabel`: `correct` | `incorrect` | `partially_correct` (legacy JSON `accept`/`reject`/`wrong_reason` normalized on read)
- `backendSignalId`: optional UUID linking a JSON signal to FastAPI `signal_predictions`
- `SignalStatus`: `new` | `reviewed` | `acted`
- Message `role`: `customer` | `agent` | `system`
- IDs: `tenant_*`, `conv_*`, `msg_*`, `sig_*`

Taxonomy SoT: `web/src/lib/taxonomy.ts`. Types: `web/src/lib/types.ts`.

## Detection (`detect.ts` + `detect-llm.ts`)

- Score **customer** messages only (ignore agent/system for matching)
- Pass 1: keyword/phrase heuristics; threshold ~0.35; top-1 (+ near-tie); structural intent patterns + fraud/complaint suppress on lead/upsell (`detect-patterns.ts`); skip locally negated phrase/keyword hits; two strong keywords clear the bar. Precision-first: ticket/chat/login/document ops and bare competitor-name mentions must not fire.
- Phrases weigh more than keywords; weak/ambiguous keywords weigh less
- Short tokens use word boundaries; `negativePhrases` in taxonomy zero that type’s score
- LLM pass (`runHybridDetection`): off unless `DETECT_LLM=1` + `GROQ_API_KEY`. Primary is the default (`DETECT_LLM_PRIMARY` not `0`): Groq classifies every chat with customer text; a grounded label replaces the heuristic hit; a failed or ungrounded call keeps the heuristic signal. `DETECT_LLM_PRIMARY=0` restores miss-only (zero heuristic signals only; never overrides a heuristic hit). Per-run candidate-chat cap (selected conversations, not provider requests): `DETECT_LLM_MAX_CALLS` when set; otherwise 8 on Vercel (`VERCEL` set) and 120 locally in primary mode; miss-only default cap is 8. Retries and daily-quota fallback add provider attempts; `DETECT_LLM_MAX_ATTEMPTS` bounds the retry loop rather than total requests (default 3, capped at 4); daily-quota fallback does not consume the retry counter. Skipped ids are stored and classified on the next re-detect before newer misses; concurrency 2; fail-soft. Default model `qwen/qwen3.8-27b`; daily-quota fallback `openai/gpt-oss-20b`
- Primary type for ranking / LLM prompt: **retention** (then upsell, then lead)
- Today `confidence === score` — do not invent a separate model score
- Suggested actions are **Shadow Mode display-only** — never execute them
- Predictions upsert on `(tenant_id, conversation_id, signal_type)` in Neon
- Unit tests: `src/lib/detect.test.ts`, `detect-patterns.test.ts`, `detect-llm.test.ts`, `ingest.test.ts`, `eval.test.ts` (`npm test`)

## Ingest / store / eval

- Ingest: first partner file (`weeklyExportCount === 0` or `replace=true`) **replaces** the JSON store (file chats only; keep tenant, taxonomyOverrides, pilot baseline). Later re-uploads **upsert** by `externalId`; chats not in this file stay; messages for a match are replaced. After replace, Neon prune of leftover `conversation_id`s is fail-soft (404 = old API)
- Formats: Sioona CSV/JSON, Intercom JSON (`conversation_parts`), WhatsApp Business `.txt` (`ingest-platforms.ts`)
- Detect **replaces** signals but **preserves SignalScore feedback** when the same `conversationId` + `type` is still emitted (`mergeSignalsPreservingFeedback`)
- Detection uses `getEffectiveTaxonomy(store.taxonomyOverrides)` — base [`taxonomy.ts`](web/src/lib/taxonomy.ts) ⊕ store overrides
- Reset reseeds from `testing.json` via `loadTestingJsonIntoStore` (empty shell in `sample-store.ts`; P/R=1.0 pack is test-only `detect-eval-fixtures.ts`)
- Optional `groundTruth` on conversations/signals for labeled eval; dual-write to Neon `conversations.ground_truth` (fail-soft); hydrate restores on cold start. Taxonomy stays JSON.
- `store.pilot.baselineOpportunities` feeds lift in `computePilotMetrics`
- Pilot pack: opportunity lift, ≥80% review precision target, go/no-go
- Demo tenant is hard-coded (`tenant_demo`) — no real multi-tenant isolation yet

## Display helpers

Signal badge colors in `format.ts`: lead=blue, retention=amber, upsell=teal. Pair color with label (never color alone).
